  "interpretation_caveats": [
    "Compare r_hat with probe/baseline rows from the ceiling table at the same checkpoint, not the larger grid table. Population and pair counts differ.",
    "Earlier all-trace rollout figures 0.626/0.655/0.811 came from 87 problems; this main-run-only table reports 0.651/0.640/0.790 from 52 problems. Treat these as different cohorts, not a direct improvement or deterioration.",
    "Do not say every early probe is at chance or recovery outperforms every probe at every checkpoint: at 512, exploratory L1 is 0.653 and r_hat is 0.651. At 2048 a recovery-target L17 probe is 0.634 versus r_hat 0.640. These layer maxima are selected from 29 comparisons.",
    "Full-grid layer20 at 8192 is 0.620 [0.54,0.71], but 29 layers and many positions are examined and the cohort changes with trace length. This is exploratory, not established onset time.",
    "The end grid uses 599 traces/103 problems, not the prior 448/87 or 636/106 populations. End L20=0.743, length=0.768, and best swept layer L25=0.775 must not be compared with earlier 0.809 or 0.829 as a controlled BOS-only effect.",
    "Original full-table raw probes use fixed C=0.1 and five GroupKFold splits, not nested layer/hyperparameter selection. Best-layer results are exploratory.",
    "Binary probes and baselines train on the full checkpoint cohort then are restricted to the main-run rollout evaluation subset. Recovery-target Ridge is trained only on the recovery subset; its differences do not isolate target choice.",
    "len_observed uses prefix paragraph count at fixed checkpoints, and paragraph count plus token count at end. len_final_oracle uses eventual n_gen and is unavailable to an online prefix monitor.",
    "Confidence intervals are separate arm intervals; no paired delta confidence intervals or p-values are supplied in these wide CSVs. A single shuffled-label probe per layer is only a sanity check.",
    "r_hat_all8 is the original script label; its loader pooled available round/sample rows without enforcing K=8, silently skipped malformed lines, and overwrote duplicate keys. Independent rollout integrity checks are required.",
    "r_hat_k1/k2/k4 are repeated subsamples of the existing rollout outcomes (20 draws), not new generation experiments; wide CSVs provide no confidence intervals for those means.",
    "End means the last trace-text token for an eligible completed trace; it is not a measured commitment point. Neither EOS identity nor activation input equality is certified by this table.",
    "The recovery sampling score is an empirical benchmark, not a proven upper bound on all probes or a certified noise ceiling.",
    "Original full extraction reused per-trace parts after checking only trace_id and layer dimension. Config has no source file hashes or token input IDs; existing source/config agreement cannot retroactively prove exact activation inputs."
  ],
